  "name": null,
  "problem": "A standard deck of $52$ cards contains $26$ red cards (hearts and diamonds) and $26$ black cards (clubs and spades). One card is drawn at random, its color is recorded, and then it is placed back in the deck before the next draw. The process is repeated until a red card is drawn. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability of finding a red card in no more than $5$ times is{{field-1}}.",
